- `Blockchain/Dev/services/vc-issuer/src/repositories/credentialRepo.ts:107-135` `getById`: `if (isDbAvailable())` then `ensureTable`, `SELECT credential FROM vc_credentials_store WHERE id = $1`; rows found returns the DB credential (line 118 region); the `catch (err: any)` at line 118 logs `'DB read failed — falling back to memory'` and does NOT rethrow; then `memoryStore.get(id)` at line 131. `memoryStore` is declared at line 28.
- `getById` has TWO callers at the base (`git grep 'getById('`): `revocationResolvers.ts:55` and `credentialRepo.ts:477` (inside `revoke`). **A change inside `getById` therefore changes `revoke()` too.** The drafter did not read `revoke` (lines 470-510). Design inside the ruling is yours: a verify-path-only read (for example a new exported function, or an option on getById) that REJECTS when the DB is available and the read throws, so `storedRecordResolver` rejects and the verifier's existing catch (`packages/shared/src/vc/verifier.ts:513-514`, `errors.push('Failed to check credential status: ...')`) turns it into verified false. Verifier ARM 1 behaviour read at `verifier.ts:492-516`: found+revoked adds an error; `!record.found` adds `'no issuer record'` (fail closed, KS-1375); a rejection adds `Failed to check credential status`.
