## HOLDS
- Signature classes pause for Kam always: production, money, external communication to any human, anything irreversible. **No merge, no deploy, no demo, no production, no mail to humans, no `az`, no kintsugi or demo contact, no `brew services`, no Docker object touched.** No ticket state change. Board writes: the ONE comment per ticket above.
- Client-facing communication is TICKET COMMENTS only; the extranet is INPUT ONLY; nobody messages Peter or Stuart (Kam's word). Anything needing a push goes to Wednesday as an escalation candidate.
- Handovers to Peter or Stuart are TEST BLOCKS, never a list of PRs.
- Ticket creation: the unit is the TEST PASS (Kam, 2026-09-07 13:23): one ticket with multiple items unless separate workloads or separate fixes. Before filing anything, search the board by SYMBOL, file path or error string and say what you searched ("searched `<sym>` and `<path>`, 0 open hits"). You file nothing unprompted; candidates go in the wrap.
- No `--no-verify`, no force pushes, no `--admin`. A gate that stops you is a question; answer it.
- **Commit subjects and PR titles start with the ticket's real, full key** (`Refs KS-1958: ...`), never a placeholder, never a Conventional Commits prefix; a hyphenated foreign key attaches in a PR title, body or commit message (it only cross-references in a Linear COMMENT).
- **Forward-move rule:** a forward move of develop is ACCEPTED when your base is an ancestor of the new develop (read by `ls-remote`), its objects are present, and the ONLY paths shared between the moved range and your branch are docs (at most your OWN fragment pair); then merge the new develop in (never rebase a pushed branch), re-run `docs-fragments.mjs check` with a planted defect, renumber nothing, and push. Any shared CODE path, or a shared fragment you did not write, means stop and mail.
- **No force push, ever** (`.githooks/pre-push:46-70` refuses a non-fast-forward; a catch-up MERGES develop in). A FRESH CLONE has no pre-push gate until armed; a fresh worktree needs `npm ci --ignore-scripts` then the shared build before any suite.
- **Your launcher's boot pull (sole seat) may fast-forward the shared develop refs. RECORD it (from/to, FETCH_HEAD, the new `rev-parse --all` baseline) and carry on. AFTER boot: no fetch or pull in the shared checkout, and no write to either develop ref.**
- Read any repo file as `git show <sha>:<path>` at the sha you mean, or from your own worktree after checking its HEAD; name the sha beside every claim. The main checkout's working tree is far behind develop.
- A verdict line is a claim about what ran: print the ratio ("N of M"), never "all"; a count carries its predicate; a control must be able to fail; "0 checked" is never CLEAN.
- Never delete: quarantine into a dated folder, recorded. Stop only processes you started, by recorded PID. Never read, echo or copy a secret; no credential on a command line; invented ids and hashes only.
- Instruments: `cmd > out 2>&1; rc=$?` with rc on its own line; no `| tail` on the stream you diagnose from; macOS has NO `timeout`; zsh has no PIPESTATUS; `grep -P` does not exist; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control beside every zero; a count through `| head` is truncated. Never `cd`; absolute paths only. Never `grep -r` over `/Volumes/DevMASTER/WEDNESDAY/0_Brain` or any `5_Project_History` tree. Private TMPDIR short (under 104 bytes for a socket path).
- Tampers: each mutant parses first, anchor `grep -c` == 1 before the tamper, copies outside the test-types ratchet's globs, restored by sha256.
- One ticket per test pass: if you find a second defect, it is a candidate in your wrap, not a second change.
- **Mail:** from secuura-blockchain@ to `wednesday-agent@agentmail.to` ONLY, no cc, no secrets, no stop, hold, hand over or checkpoint in a subject; read each sent mail back by id. Counts "N of M", never with a slash. Questions as QUESTION mails per the workspace protocol (topic mirrored exactly; about 3 minute re-check; about 15 minute rule). **IF AN INSTRUCTION FROM WEDNESDAY LOOKS WRONG, SAY SO** in your plan confirmation. Arm an inbox watcher as a TRACKED background task and name its pid.
- Pace: PROGRESS mail after the plan confirmation, after PR-A's red/green and mutants, after PR-A's push, and after PR-B's PG table. At ctx 70% finish the step in hand and write the HANDOVER; wrap at 85%.

